#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Les moutons (story 111, cycle 59; a hook, a law of the story stated in line 4, an escalation through the whole country, a reversal, a loop ending).
This man cannot sleep, so he counts sheep. In the morning there are four thousand of them in his bedroom, for real. Their bleating wakes the
building, which counts in turn, and the loop runs away: the more they count, the less they sleep, and the less they sleep, the more they count. The
sheep fill the stairwell, the street, then the town, white as under snow. Wool is worth nothing: a herbal tea buys a flock. Only the shepherds sleep,
standing up: they are used to it. The whole country counts, so far that nobody knows what comes next. An accountant finds the answer: count
backwards. On TV the whole country counts down, three, two, one, and not one sheep is left, neither on the farms nor in the jumpers. Except the black
sheep, who does as it pleases: it cannot sleep either, so it counts the guys, and this guy, for real, jumps the fence four thousand times a night.
Running gag (never said): the black sheep is the last sheep he counts in S01b, and from then on it is in every sheep shot (S01b, S02b, S06b, S09b,
S12c, S13, S13b, S14, S15, S16) and never sleeps until the last shot: an ordinary charcoal-fleeced sheep (mtSheep black: the series' creature sheep
recoloured, oversized white eyes with thick red rims and grey bags, no glow), always three quarters to us, staring at him, and above its head a white
thought bubble (mtBubble) in which a tiny box-headed man in a dark suit and a red tie hops a little white fence, leaning forward (S06b, S09b),
then panting (S13b, S14) more each time. S15 goes into the bubble, S16 makes it real: the fence of S01 is back, the man is him, and the black sheep
counts him with nods until it falls asleep, smiling, a snot bubble at its nose. Second marker: his bed rides the sheep wave out of the building
(S05b) and drops back onto the cobbles only when the last sheep vanishes (S12). By ear « n'arrivait pas à dormir » (S01) comes back in « Lui non plus
n'arrivait pas à dormir » (S14), « Il a compté les moutons » (S01b) in « il a compté les mecs » (S15), « quatre mille » (S02b) in the last line.
« Mouton noir » is only ever an animal: it is never rejected by the flock, no line reads it as a person.
Staging (natural look; a cut every 0.9 to 2.4 s, long lines split into b/c shots on their words):
S01 his bedroom by night, deep blue, the bedside lamp on: straight over the bed, his face the right way up, he lies stiff, arms down his sides, eyes
wide on the ceiling; a twitch runs down him (a stretch, the eyes spring wider, no blink on it), his eyes dart left and right, a blink; a pop off screen
at the foot of the bed (the fence): his eyes snap down, his head lifts and he nods (count one). S01b his point of view down the bed (the camera nods on
each count): beyond the foot of the bed a little white fence stands at an angle; white sheep hop it toward him; the last one is the black sheep: it
lands, stops dead with a squash, turns to him (to us) three quarters and stares; the bubble pops above its head. S02 morning, high over the room from
its open side: packed to the top of the walls with fleece blobs like a ball pit; the whole mass heaves with a chorus bleat, a sheep bursts up out of
it beside his box head, which rides up and down on top; the black sheep's head pokes out behind. S02b close on his head
in the wool: grey rings under his eyes, a sheep sits down on his head (his head squashes under it) and chews; beyond, the only dark head, the black
sheep, buried to the chin, stares at him, bubble on; he rolls his eyes up to the sheep, then to us, one slow blink. S03 a block of flats cut open on
three flats stacked, a bed in each, feet toward us: three neighbours asleep; BÊÊ: all three spring up off their mattresses stiff as planks, stretched,
eyes wide, and land sitting with a squash; the bottom one claps his hands over his ears, the top one's hair stands on end. S03b closer: the same
three sitting up in bed; a fence pops up beside each bed and a sheep hops each; their eyes go to it and the three nod in sync on each count, lips
moving (lying, seen from the foot of the beds, a nod did not read). S04 one
neighbour's bedroom: a sheep hops the fence beside his bed and bleats; his eyes snap wider; he nods faster; a second sheep, a louder bleat, his eyes
bigger, pinpoint pupils. S04b lower and closer: a third sheep, the loudest bleat; fleece blobs pop up round the bed, higher and higher, the bed
squashes and sinks under the heap; only his hand sticks out, still pumping the count. S05 the stairwell, one flight from the side, a blue-grey wall: a white wave
of fleece slides down the steps like a conveyor (the lower steps still bare), three sheep riding its front, the concierge surfing down on top of it
sideways, facing us, still sweeping with her broom.
S05b the street: the building's door bursts open, a white tongue of fleece slides out with blobs bobbing on it, and his bed rides out on it like a
raft, him still lying in it, eyes open, nodding. S06 high over the rooftops: a wave of fleece pops onto the roofs and the street from far to near,
everything white; a snowplough far down the street. S06b street level: the plough passes behind pushing a big fleece roll; three sheep hop back over
its cab; in front, above the captions, the black sheep sits on a bench, wide awake, bubble on: the little man now leans forward. S07 a market stall in
the white street (an awning, a teapot, cups; no lettering, no price): a man in pyjamas holds a rope leading five sheep; the stallholder picks up a
fleece blob, sniffs, and flicks it over his shoulder onto the heap behind (worthless). S07b the man hands over the rope, takes one steaming cup of
herbal tea, sips: his eyelids drop shut at once and he sleeps standing, swaying; the stallholder loops the rope on his post. S08 the street flooded
with fleece to the knees: a shepherd (cape, wide felt hat, crook) asleep standing up, leaning on his crook, smiling, a snot bubble swelling and
shrinking; his chest swells and sinks with each snore. S08b three sheep hop over him in an arc, the last lands on his hat (the hat squashes, his head
dips); he does not stir. S09 night over a street, every window lit: in the two nearest windows two big silhouettes in pyjamas count with nods, stop,
frown at each other, start again (INSOMNIE). S09b low on the nearest roof, looking up: the black sheep sits on the ridge with the
big moon right behind its head (a dark sheep reads only against it), tired red-rimmed eyes, its head drooping and snapping back up, bubble on. S10 an accountant at his desk in his living room by lamplight (green eyeshade, sleeve protectors, grey rings
under the eyes), a little fence and one small sheep on the desk: he flips his thick ledger backwards, pages fanning back to front (ruled lines, no
figures), and his eyes light up. S10b the sheep hops backwards over the fence in a reversed arc and vanishes in a puff; he points at us in triumph,
then yawns enormously. S11 a TV studio (a plain desk, a blue backdrop with a big plain white sheep shape; no text, no figures): a presenter in a bow
tie and a cream wool jumper speaks, conducting with a pencil. S11b a living room: a family of four in woolly jumpers on the sofa nods on each beat of
the countdown, and on the floor in front of them one sheep vanishes in a puff on each nod (DÉCOMPTE). S12 the white street: the fleece shrinks to
nothing, puffs on the nearest blobs, the bench and the plough come back; his bed drops the last metre onto the cobbles with a squash, him in it. S12b
the farm: the shepherd wakes with a start in an empty field, his crook alone in his hand; beside him the last farm sheep vanishes mid-chew; a farmer
drops his milk pail, the milk splashes. S12c the living room: the four jumpers pop off into nothing, four puffs, the family left in white shirts, arms
crossed, shivering; on the last puff a black sheep's head pops up into the empty foreground. S13 the empty street, grey and green again: the black
sheep alone in the middle of the road plants its hooves with a stomp, chin up. S13b closer: it shakes its head slowly, no, chin up, eyes red-rimmed,
bubble on, the little man panting. S14 a meadow at night, seen from its side: the black sheep lies on its back, hooves in the air, eyes wide
on the stars (his pose of S01), tapping a hoof on its belly. S15 a push in on its bubble until it fills the frame: on a moonlit meadow the little man hops
the fence, runs round, hops again; the black sheep in the corner nods once at each hop. S16 the meadow, for real, the fence of S01: he runs in, in his
suit, rings down to his chin, and jumps it clean (a crouch, a stretched take-off, legs tucked, the tie flying, a squash on landing); at the top he
sees the black sheep nod (count one) and takes: BOING, a puff of white fleece bursts out of his head, eyes wide with pinpoint pupils; he lands. S16b
wider: he jogs round in a loop and jumps again, panting, a sweat drop, the fleece bobbing on his head; the black sheep nods, its eyelids drooping. S16c
the black sheep has shut its eyes and snores, smiling, its snot bubble swelling and shrinking; behind it he jumps the fence again. Hold.
Props (engine/props_moutons.js, cycle 59): mtSheep, mtFleece, mtFence, mtBubble, mtWoolHair, mtPlough, mtStall, mtCup, mtRope, mtCape, mtFeltHat,
mtCrook, mtEyeshade, mtSleeve, mtLedger, mtDeskLamp, mtStudio, mtBowTie, mtPencil, mtJumper, mtKnitSleeve, mtNightWindow, mtNightRow, mtMoon, mtPail,
mtMilk, mtPuff, mtBlob; reused: moCutaway, moStairs, moFacade, moRoof, moLamp, moRoom (props_mot), seGroundCut (props_sel), bed, desk, chair, door,
bench, broom, stars (props.js); sets chambre (poster False), cottageStreet, livingRoom (carpet False), farm, grassland, whiteVoid. Never the lab (its
board shows a formula and figures) nor the office (« OBJECTIFS Q3 », « +12% »).
Lessons applied from the start: Looney deformation on every accent (squash and stretch on every hop, landing, pop and puff, the plank spring of the
neighbours, the heaving fleece, the rubber flick, the snore that swells the shepherd, the woolly take); every action starts in the first 0.3 s of its
shot; one fresh take for the hero at the twist (S16: a fleece puff bursts out of his head, no eyes on stalks, no spiked hair); blinks, breathing and
glances on every hold (life()); carried props are one world prop attached to the hand that carries them (broom, crook, cup, pencil, pail), handed
over by an attach key; look targets at head height or the camera, pupils for the rest; word timings from timeline.json through st.at (words from 0,
printed beside their times); every cut set just under its frame (floor(round(t*30)/30*1e4)/1e4); cameras fitted with fit()/fitBack() at a margin of
0.12 to 0.2 and checked with project() (CHECKS, and BANDS warnings: heads out of the caption band 0.77-0.83 and the card band 0.07-0.18); every flat
thing on a floor has a polygon offset or a gap of 10 cm or more, and the street's ground disc is cut under its road (seGroundCut); at most five
rigged sheep and five people per shot, the masses are faceless fleece blobs; the sheep are clearly sheep (white fleece, black face and legs, a round
body), the black one an ordinary dark-fleeced sheep; counting by nods and voice only (no digits, no tally); new props prefixed mt; sound names
checked against audio3.py, audio.py and mix.py; no organisation, brand, flag, emblem, cross, insignia, digit or currency on screen; French only
(INSOMNIE, DÉCOMPTE are the cards); people keep their shirts on when the jumpers vanish; nobody hurt.
Round 1 corrections (critics 7.0 / 6.8): S16-S16c the jumps run ACROSS the frame (the fence at 55 degrees), a held crouch, a long arc over the fence,
a landing squash, his head to the lens at the top, him about a quarter of the frame tall; the film ends with him in the air. The black sheep by night
(S14-S16c) has a pale moonlit rim, a soft key light and a pale moonlit patch of meadow behind it (the meadow lighter); S14 seen from above its head,
both eyes to the lens, a big drumming tap; the bubble's sheep a third of the bubble wide, nodding. One fleece everywhere: round lobes with smooth
shading, a curl pattern, cool white, a thin slate outline, the rigged sheep's bodies included. S01 the fence pops up out of the blanket at his feet;
S01b the white sheep leave before the black one lands. S03 the block by night with facades, lit windows and a roof, a 2-frame jolt with an overshoot.
S04 / S10 a multiple-image frame (buzz under a short shutter) and eyes out for 2-3 frames. S07 the stallholder in front of his stall, the flock coming
toward the lens. S12b one lead action (the last sheep vanishes beside the pail). S12c clean white shirts appear, neutral puffs thrown sideways."""
from story_kit import *
import math

st = Story('moutons', look='natural')
st.plan([('S01', 'L01', 0), ('S01b', 1.3, 0), ('S02', 'L02', 0), ('S02b', 'L02', 4), ('S03', 'L03', 0), ('S03b', 'L03', 5), ('S04', 'L04', 0), ('S04b', 'L04', 6),
         ('S05', 'L05', 0), ('S05b', 14.3, 0), ('S06', 'L06', 0), ('S06b', 'L06', 3), ('S07', 'L07', 0), ('S07b', 'L07', 6), ('S08', 'L08', 0), ('S08b', 'L08', 4),
         ('S09', 'L09', 0), ('S09b', 'L09', 4), ('S10', 'L10', 0), ('S10b', 'L10', 4), ('S11', 'L11', 0), ('S11b', 31.35, 0), ('S12', 'L12', 0), ('S12b', 'L12', 4),
         ('S12c', 'L12', 8), ('S13', 'L13', 0), ('S13b', 'L13', 4), ('S14', 'L14', 0), ('S15', 'L15', 0), ('S16', 'L16', 0), ('S16b', 'L16', 5), ('S16c', 46.0, 0)])
# every cut just under its frame: st.cut rounds to 4 decimals (after the frame: its first image would show the shot before); take the frame index and
# floor its time instead
FL = lambda v: math.floor(round(v * 30) / 30 * 10000) / 10000
st.SH = {sid: (FL(a), FL(b) if b < st.total else b) for sid, (a, b) in st.SH.items()}

PI = math.pi
def r(v, n=3): return round(v, n)
def add(a, b): return [r(a[i] + b[i]) for i in range(3)]
def lerp3(a, b, u): return [r(a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * u) for i in range(3)]
def yaw(src, dst): return r(math.degrees(math.atan2(dst[0] - src[0], dst[2] - src[2])), 1)
def fwd(ry): return [math.sin(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.cos(math.radians(ry))]
def right(ry): return [-math.cos(math.radians(ry)), 0.0, math.sin(math.radians(ry))]
def off(p, ry, f=0.0, s=0.0, y=0.0): F, R = fwd(ry), right(ry); return [r(p[0] + F[0] * f + R[0] * s), r(p[1] + y), r(p[2] + F[2] * f + R[2] * s)]
CHECKS = []
def chk(sid, frm, look, lens, pts, heads=()):
    pr = {n: project(frm, look, lens, p) for n, p in pts.items()}
    CHECKS.append(f"{sid}: " + ' | '.join(f"{n} {v}" for n, v in pr.items()))
    for n in heads:
        v = pr.get(n)
        if not v or not (0 <= v[0] <= 1 and 0 <= v[1] <= 1): CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} out of the frame {v}")
        elif 0.77 <= v[1] <= 0.83: CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} in the caption band {v}")
        elif 0.07 <= v[1] <= 0.18: CHECKS.append(f"  BANDS {sid}: {n} in the card band {v}")
def chkc(sid, c, pts, heads=(), end=False):
    frm, look = (c.get('to') or c['from'], c.get('lookAt2') or c['lookAt']) if end else (c['from'], c['lookAt'])
    chk(sid + ('>' if end else ''), frm, look, c['lens'], pts, heads)
def chk2(sid, c, pts, heads=()): chkc(sid, c, pts, heads); chkc(sid, c, pts, heads, end=True)
def W(sid, lid, i):
    # word timings from timeline.json: st.at counts the words from 0; the word is printed beside its time
    t = st.at(sid, lid, i); CHECKS.append(f"{sid} « {st.L[lid]['words'][i]['w']} » at {t}"); return t
def R5(p, w=1, s=0.0): return [*p, w, s]
def FIT(frm, pts, back=False, **kw):
    # the aim and the lens that hold every point (a margin of 0.12-0.2 of the width, above the captions): fit() / fitBack() of the kit
    kw.setdefault('margin', 0.14); kw.setdefault('top', 0.12); kw.setdefault('bottom', 0.76); kw.setdefault('lenses', range(28, 57))
    if back: f, look, lens = fitBack(frm, pts, **kw)
    else:
        f = frm; look, lens, _ = fit(frm, pts, **{k_: v for k_, v in kw.items() if k_ not in ('inside', 'level')})
        if not lens: f, look, lens = fitBack(frm, pts, **kw)
    assert lens, f'no lens fits from {frm}'
    return [r(v) for v in f], [r(v) for v in look], lens
def CAM(frm, look, lens, push=0.15, at=0.0, ease='inOut', dy=0.0):
    # a slow push in along the aim (every framing moves a little)
    d = [look[i] - frm[i] for i in range(3)]; n = math.sqrt(sum(v * v for v in d)) or 1
    return cam(at, frm, [r(frm[i] + d[i] / n * push + (dy if i == 1 else 0)) for i in range(3)], look, look, lens=lens, ease=ease)
def HAND(R=None, L=None, hr='rest', hl='rest', tipR=0.0, tipL=0.0, **x):
    return {'reach': {**({'R': R5(R, 1, tipR)} if R else {}), **({'L': R5(L, 1, tipL)} if L else {})}, 'hands': {'R': hr, 'L': hl}, 'hip': 0, **x}
def blink(t, face, keep=None): return [k(t, toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': {**face, 'lid': 1.0}}, toonDur=0.05), k(r(t + 0.1), toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': face}, toonDur=0.06)]
def life(t0, t1, face, keep=None, ph=0.0, blinks=(), period=0.9, amp=0.013, glance=None):
    # a moving hold: slow breathing keys that carry the face and the hands (a toon key is a whole state), clear of the blinks; glance (gx) on every
    # other breath when given
    out, bl, t_, i = [], sorted(blinks), t0 + ph, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.08:
        if not any(-0.04 < t_ - b < 0.2 for b in bl):
            q = [r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4), r(1 + amp, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.4, 4)] if i % 2 == 0 else [r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4), r(1 - amp * 0.6, 4), r(1 + amp * 0.3, 4)]
            fc = {**face, **({'gx': glance * (1 if i % 4 < 2 else -1)} if glance else {})}
            out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'sq': q, 'face': fc}, toonDur=r(period * 0.8), toonEase='inOut'))
        t_ += period / 2; i += 1
    for b in bl: out += blink(r(b), face, keep)
    return out
def TALK(t0, t1, face, keep=None, step=0.1, nod=0.05, tilt=0.0):
    # lip flaps (open / o / line shapes, small nods); keep: the hands (a toon key is a whole state)
    out, t_, i = [], t0, 0
    while t_ < t1 - 0.04:
        m = ['open', 'o', 'line', 'open', 'smirk'][i % 5]
        bd = {**(keep or {}).get('bend', {}), 'neck': [r(nod if i % 3 == 0 else -nod * 0.5), tilt, 0, 1, None]}
        out.append(k(r(t_), toon={**(keep or {}), 'bend': bd, 'face': {**face, 'mouth': m, 'jaw': 0.25 if m in ('open', 'o') else 0.0}}, toonDur=r(step * 0.7)))
        t_ += step; i += 1
    return out
def NODS(times, face, keep=None, amt=0.32, lying=False, talk=True):
    # one nod per count: the chin drops (the head lifts when he lies on his back) and comes back, the lips move on it
    out = []
    for t in times:
        bd = {**(keep or {}).get('bend', {})}
        bd['neck'] = [r(amt * (1.4 if lying else 1.0)), 0, 0, 1, None]
        out += [k(r(t - 0.04), toon={**(keep or {}), 'bend': bd, 'face': {**face, **({'mouth': 'O', 'jaw': 0.3} if talk else {})}}, toonDur=0.06, toonEase='out'),
                k(r(t + 0.12), toon={**(keep or {}), 'face': {**face, 'mouth': 'line'}}, toonDur=0.1)]
    return out
SEED = iter(range(11101, 11199))

# ============================== sheep, fence, bubble, fleece
def SHEEP(pid, pos, ry=0.0, keys=None, **o): return P(pid, 'mtSheep', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, opts={'seed': next(SEED), **o}, **({'keys': keys} if keys else {}))
def BLACK(pid, pos, ry=0.0, keys=None, **o): return P(pid, 'mtSheep', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, opts={'black': True, 'seed': 7, **o}, **({'keys': keys} if keys else {}))
def FENCE(pid, pos, ry=0.0, **o): return P(pid, 'mtFence', pos=list(pos), ry=ry, opts=o)
def BUBBLE(pid, pos, face_to, **o): return P(pid, 'mtBubble', pos=list(pos), ry=yaw(pos, face_to), opts=o)
def FLEECE(pid, fill, keys=None, **o): return P(pid, 'mtFleece', pos=[0, 0, 0], opts={'fill': fill, **o}, **({'keys': keys} if keys else {}))
def HOP(t0, dur, to, h=0.55): return [r(t0), r(dur), [r(v) for v in to], h]
def turn_to(pos, ry_prop, target, extra=0.0):
    # the body yaw (radians, relative to the prop's ry) that faces target, plus extra degrees (three quarters)
    return r(math.radians(yaw(pos, target) - ry_prop + extra), 3)
BUBH = 0.62   # the bubble's middle above a sheep's head (m, at size 1)

# ============================== the hero
HF = {'lid': 0.0, 'eye': 0.3, 'mouth': 'line', 'brow': 0.4, 'bags': 0.8, 'expr': 'surprised', 'exprW': 0.75}   # wide awake (his painted lids are heavy: a surprised base opens them), rings under the eyes
GAGS = [('S01', 0.12, 'mec', 'twitch'), ('S01b', 0.55, 'mec', 'counts'), ('S02b', 0.2, 'mec', 'sheep sits on head'), ('S03', 0.25, 'v1', 'plank spring'),
        ('S04', 1.3, 'v2', 'eyes bigger'), ('S05', 0.7, 'concierge', 'surfs'), ('S05b', 0.6, 'mec', 'bed raft'), ('S07', 0.6, 'marchand', 'flick'),
        ('S07b', 0.9, 'pyjama', 'falls asleep'), ('S08', 0.6, 'berger', 'snore'), ('S08b', 0.9, 'berger', 'sheep on hat'), ('S10', 0.7, 'comptable', 'ledger'),
        ('S10b', 0.75, 'comptable', 'points'), ('S11', 0.5, 'presentateur', 'conducts'), ('S11b', 1.1, 'pere', 'nods'), ('S12', 0.75, 'mec', 'bed drops'),
        ('S12b', 0.3, 'berger', 'wakes'), ('S12c', 0.5, 'mere', 'shiver')]
for g_ in GAGS: st.gag(*g_)

NIGHT_IN = {'sun': 0.35, 'sunColor': '#9DB4EC', 'fill': 0.75, 'exposure': 1.0}
NIGHT_OUT = {'sun': 0.3, 'sunColor': '#9DB4EC', 'fill': 0.7, 'exposure': 0.95}
ROOM_N = {'poster': False, 'clutter': False, 'wall': '#3E5486', 'band': '#33456E', 'floor': '#7A6650', 'pane': '#22346A', 'paneGlow': '#0E1A40', 'curtain': '#6A4A7A', 'blanket': '#8A9ACC'}
ROOM_D = {'poster': False, 'clutter': False, 'wall': '#8FB2DE', 'band': '#7A9CC8', 'pane': '#E8F6FF', 'paneGlow': '#9ACCEE', 'curtain': '#6A4A7A', 'blanket': '#8A9ACC'}
BED = [-2.6, 0.0, -1.9]                     # the chambre's bed (pillow toward -Z)
HB = add(BED, [0, 0.52, 0.2])               # his hips lying in it
HEADL = add(BED, [0, 0.82, -0.62])          # his face lying on the pillow
LAMP = [-1.75, 0.0, -2.62]

# 1: « Ce mec n'arrivait pas à dormir. » His bedroom by night, deep blue, the lamp on; high over the bed, looking down on his face from the foot side: he
#    lies stiff, arms down his sides, eyes wide on the ceiling; a twitch runs down him (a stretch, the eyes spring wider), his eyes dart left and right,
